      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Late miss",
          "heading": "Paolo Garbisi misses late penalty touch kick as Argentina edge Italy 19-14",
          "body": "Italy fly-half Paolo Garbisi missed a penalty touch kick in the closing moments of Saturday's Genoa test, the attempt meant to set up a lineout in a scoring position, and Argentina held on to win 19-14. Italy had been reduced to 14 men after substitute lock Efrain Elias was shown a yellow card, yet a penalty try had brought them back within five points after winger Monty Ioane's early try. Planet Rugby noted that Garbisi had the chance to clinch a first victory over Argentina in 18 years."
        },
        {
