          "kicker": "Defensive display",
          "heading": "James Botham and Jac Morgan spearhead Wales defence that repelled All Blacks",
          "body": "Saturday's 35-28 win over New Zealand was settled as much at the back as in attack. With New Zealand flanker Peter Lakai's late try cutting the margin to seven, Wales' defenders held firm in the final quarter, and WalesOnline described the effort as miraculous, with Gareth Thomas, James Botham, Jac Morgan, Dafydd Jenkins and Eddie James all singled out. Wales made more than 300 tackles, and the All Blacks had 65 per cent of the possession, according to Planet Rugby."
        },
