          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Carter Gordon recalled at flyhalf as Les Kiss restores Rob Valetini",
          "body": "Carter Gordon is back at No 10 for Sunday's clash with Scotland, and Australia coach Les Kiss sees him as the answer to a jersey that has had seven different starters since the last World Cup. Gordon is back from a broken leg and was building into the role before the Argentina injury. Rob Valetini returns at six, with Declan Meredith dropped from the match-day 23. \"Certainly Carter was the incumbent, so he was in a position of strength before he got injured,\" Kiss said."
        },
